# Security

## Framework semantics

CakePHP security spans mass assignment, FormProtection/CSRF, authentication vs authorization, safe SQL, uploads, serialization, redirects, secrets, and debug exposure. Prefer framework middleware/components already configured in the app over inventing parallel token schemes.

## Required behavior

- Keep Entity mass assignment tight (`_accessible` / field lists).
- Enforce authorization on the server; never only in the UI.
- Distinguish authentication (identity) from authorization (permission).
- For HTML forms, use CakePHP FormProtection / CSRF middleware as the project already wires them — do not rely on client-only tokens.
- Validate and store uploads with explicit type/size/path rules; never trust client filenames as filesystem paths.
- Prefer ORM Query expressions and bindings; never concatenate untrusted input into SQL (`unsafe-sql-concatenation`, `orm-vs-connection-sql`).
- Do not leak secrets in logs, exceptions, or serialized outputs (`$_hidden`, API shaping).
- Keep credentials and API keys in config/env — never commit them.
- Reject open redirects: only redirect to known-safe local routes/paths.
- Keep `debug` disabled in production; do not expose stack traces or DebugKit in prod.
- Prefer `password_hash` / Authentication password hashers over reversible encoding for passwords.

## Anti-patterns

- Mass assignment overexposure
- Authorization only in UI
- Serialization overexposure
- Missing FormProtection/CSRF on state-changing HTML forms
- CSRF-only-in-javascript
- unsafe-upload-handling
- unsafe-sql-concatenation
- Open redirects from user-supplied URLs
- Debug-in-production
- Secrets in source control or logs

## Review checklist

- [ ] Write endpoints check server-side authz / IDOR scoping
- [ ] Forms participate in project FormProtection/CSRF setup
- [ ] Uploads are validated and stored outside webroot when required
- [ ] Sensitive fields hidden from default serialization
- [ ] Redirect targets are allow-listed / local
- [ ] Production debug/DebugKit off; secrets not logged
- [ ] No unbound SQL concatenation; prefer ORM bindings
